{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01414",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.04,
      "end_seconds": 5.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. I've settled them in, ready when you are."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.0,
      "end_seconds": 10.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Perfect, thanks. Hello there, so what's the trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 11.72,
      "end_seconds": 19.08,
      "duration_seconds": 7.36,
      "text": "Good afternoon, you know, doctor. I look after them so I thought I'd come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.86,
      "end_seconds": 22.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Please do. Extra information is always welcome."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.22,
      "end_seconds": 31.72,
      "duration_seconds": 7.5,
      "text": "I've been getting out of breath on the stairs, and I wanted to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.0,
      "end_seconds": 38.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.82,
      "end_seconds": 42.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Around two weeks, I think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 44.13,
      "end_seconds": 47.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "It was closer to three weeks, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.32,
      "end_seconds": 54.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly two to three weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.02,
      "end_seconds": 57.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "Yeah, roughly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.35,
      "end_seconds": 67.7,
      "duration_seconds": 9.35,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.02,
      "end_seconds": 72.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "I notice it more with stairs. Severe, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.88,
      "end_seconds": 80.08,
      "duration_seconds": 6.2,
      "text": "I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 80.18,
      "end_seconds": 86.73,
      "duration_seconds": 6.55,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.52,
      "end_seconds": 89.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Later, thanks. Please go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.91,
      "end_seconds": 104.16,
      "duration_seconds": 12.25,
      "text": "And I've been feeling tired all the time as well, for two months. As for feeling tired all the time, it feels mild to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.34,
      "end_seconds": 110.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "Have you noticed black stools, weight loss or heavy periods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.07,
      "end_seconds": 125.3,
      "duration_seconds": 11.23,
      "text": "No, no black stools, no weight loss, no heavy periods. I was looking pale at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.23,
      "end_seconds": 129.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.51,
      "end_seconds": 135.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.15,
      "end_seconds": 157.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.05,
      "end_seconds": 163.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "My cousin has psoriasis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.95,
      "end_seconds": 167.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.94,
      "end_seconds": 173.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.46,
      "end_seconds": 175.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "And your job?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.45,
      "end_seconds": 179.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "I work in accounts at a hospital."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.89,
      "end_seconds": 185.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.55,
      "end_seconds": 204.3,
      "duration_seconds": 17.75,
      "text": "I have arthritis in my knees, for nearly five years. Yeah, I've had low haemoglobin, yes. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.85,
      "end_seconds": 206.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "I see, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.34,
      "end_seconds": 212.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "I have an underactive thyroid, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.77,
      "end_seconds": 224.27,
      "duration_seconds": 11.5,
      "text": "Alright, low haemoglobin and an underactive thyroid, that matches what I have here. Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.49,
      "end_seconds": 231.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "I'm allergic to nickel, I get a rash on my skin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.02,
      "end_seconds": 235.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Any surgery in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.14,
      "end_seconds": 242.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "I had a caesarean for my second baby nine years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.56,
      "end_seconds": 247.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.41,
      "end_seconds": 253.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Ah, I take paracetamol, 650 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 254.34,
      "end_seconds": 261.68,
      "duration_seconds": 7.34,
      "text": "She is supposed to take it when needed, but I can't say she always does."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.38,
      "end_seconds": 265.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "It's iron tablets, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.57,
      "end_seconds": 274.79,
      "duration_seconds": 8.22,
      "text": "It's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a small white one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.46,
      "end_seconds": 278.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.31,
      "end_seconds": 291.11,
      "duration_seconds": 11.8,
      "text": "For my thyroid, I believe. My husband sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. A multivitamin. I take it daily."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 298.17,
      "end_seconds": 312.45,
      "duration_seconds": 14.28,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Weight 63 kilos, respiratory rate 18, height 163 centimetres, blood pressure 115 over 77, SpO2 96 percent on room air, heart rate 110, BMI works out to 23.7."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.59,
      "end_seconds": 315.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.85,
      "end_seconds": 321.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.71,
      "end_seconds": 327.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "Yes, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.32,
      "end_seconds": 331.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 345.84,
      "end_seconds": 351.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.78,
      "text": "Your inner eyelids look pale and your pulse is a little fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.48,
      "end_seconds": 376.33,
      "duration_seconds": 18.85,
      "text": "You can sit up now. Having listened and examined, I can't pin this down yet. We're looking at tiredness probably from low iron or an underactive thyroid. Low vitamin B12 is still possible. I want a thyroid test done, that's for tiredness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 377.17,
      "end_seconds": 380.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "I can book that for Monday at 10 am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 381.72,
      "end_seconds": 397.02,
      "duration_seconds": 15.3,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an iron study for pallor. Take the iron with orange juice, not with tea. Come back after the results. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 398.68,
      "end_seconds": 401.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "No, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 402.4,
      "end_seconds": 403.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "Take care now."
    }
  ]
}